issue_title:
JSoup parsing unclosed tags

raw_response:
Looking at the error message, the test expects `<a href="http://example.com/">Error link</a>` but gets `<a>Error link</a>` - the href attribute is missing from the reconstructed anchor element.

The bug is in the Adoption Agency Algorithm section. When a new `adopter` element is created to replace the formatting element, it copies the tag but not the attributes:

```java
Element adopter = new Element(formatEl.tag(), tb.getBaseUri());
```

This creates a new element with the same tag name but without any attributes from `formatEl`. The `href` attribute gets lost.

The fix is to also copy the attributes from `formatEl` to the `adopter`.

Also, I notice two other bugs:
1. `StringUtil.in("optgroup", "option")` - missing `name` variable
2. `StringUtil.in("rp", "rt")` - missing `name` variable

But the primary bug causing the test failure is the missing attributes on the adopter element.

