Looking at the failing test, it's trying to deserialize `"[ "xyz", { } ]"` into `String[].class` and expects the exception to have a path reference with index 1.

The bug is that the `deserialize` and `_deserializeCustom` methods don't track the array index, so when an exception is thrown, no reference information is added to the path.

The fix requires wrapping the deserialization loop with try-catch to catch exceptions and add index reference information, similar to how other array deserializers work.

