Unable to select a pure long option in a group

raw_response:
Looking at the issue, when options are created with only a long option (using `withLongOpt`), `option.getOpt()` returns `null` (since there's no short option key set). 

The bug is in `setSelected`: when `option.getOpt()` returns `null`, `selected = option.getOpt()` sets `selected` to `null`, making it appear nothing was selected. Additionally, the condition `selected.equals(option.getOpt())` would compare with `null`.

The fix should use `option.getLongOpt()` as a fallback when `option.getOpt()` is `null`, to properly store and compare the selected option identifier.

```json
{
  "fixed_function": "public void setSelected(Option option) throws AlreadySelectedException
{
    if (option == null)
    {
        // reset the option previously selected
        selected = null;
        return;
    }

    // if no option has already been selected or the 
    // same option is being reselected then set the
    // selected member variable
    String key = option.getKey();
    if (selected == null || selected.equals(key))
    {
        selected = key;
    }
    else
    {
        throw new AlreadySelectedException(this, option);
